{"name":"Old Piano Keys","hex":"#efeedc","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"old","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mochi."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an object, concept, relationship, etc., having existed for a relatively long period of time.","Of a living being, having lived for most of the expected years."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old"},{"term":"piano","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A percussive keyboard musical instrument, usually ranging over seven octaves, with white and black colored keys, played by pressing these keys, causing hammers to strike strings. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To play the piano.","To move (the fingers) up and down on, similar to the motions of a pianist playing the piano."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/piano"},{"term":"keys","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of key","keyboard"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of key"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keys"}],"entries":[{"title":"Keys (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Keys is the eighth studio album by American singer and songwriter Alicia Keys, released through RCA Records on December 10, 2021; her last album released under the label as they parted ways in the summer of 2022. It was primarily produced by Keys. It was preceded by the release of two singles: \"Lala\" featuring Swae Lee and \"Best of Me\". The album was announced on October 27 and includes two discs, with two versions of 10 tracks, along with six other tracks."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2a/Alicia_Keys_-_Keys.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keys_(album)","wikidata":"Q109545636"},{"title":"Key (instrument)","blocks":[{"text":"A key is a component of a musical instrument, the purpose and function of which depends on the instrument. However, the term is most often used in the context of keyboard instruments, in which case it refers to the exterior part of the instrument that the player physically interacts in the process of sound production."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Steinway_Schriftzug.jpg/330px-Steinway_Schriftzug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Key_(instrument)","wikidata":"Q1117156"},{"title":"Piano","blocks":[{"text":"A piano is a keyboard instrument that produces sound when its keys are pressed, activating an action mechanism where hammers strike strings. Modern pianos have a row of 88 black and white keys—with the exception of the Bosendörfer and Stuart & Sons pianos—and tuned to a chromatic scale in equal temperament. A musician who specializes in piano is called a pianist."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Steinway_Vienna_002.JPG/330px-Steinway_Vienna_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piano","wikidata":"Q5994"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2a/Alicia_Keys_-_Keys.png/250px-Alicia_Keys_-_Keys.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2a/Alicia_Keys_-_Keys.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2a/Alicia_Keys_-_Keys.png/250px-Alicia_Keys_-_Keys.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlicia_Keys_-_Keys.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Steinway_Schriftzug.jpg/500px-Steinway_Schriftzug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=